+## 2026-10-23T17:17:55.1209892+08:00 (UTC+08:00) - Recover queued writes after SQLite automatic FULL rollback
+
+- Reproduced permanent flush suspension in provider .3 with its actual embedded Xerial driver and a real page-capped SQLite file. FULL aborts the entire native transaction, while JDBC retains manual-commit configuration; a second rollback fails and permanently fences retained writes after capacity returns.
+- Provider .4 observes native SQLite rollback/commit hooks only during each serialized flush. A pre-commit typed SQLITE_FULL with observed rollback, no commit callback, and current/next DEFERRED mode may reopen a native DEFERRED transaction before retry. Failed transaction restart, other drivers/wrappers/modes, uncertain commits and unreconstructable legacy batches preserve the existing fence. No error-message matching or queue replacement is used; listeners are removed in finally.
+- Fresh :neoforge:build succeeds with Java 21 in a separate artifact checkout/cache. Actual-provider standalone suite passes 93 assertions, including repeated ordinary/batch FULL aborts, exact original prefix/null/owned 32KiB binary/later write recovery, mode fences, typed FULL after real commit, legacy batches and the preceding lock/concurrency regressions. Native validation is recorded separately by the parent project. The physical drive is not filled and no production files are activated.
